In this folder, we provide notebooks that use the functions located in the codes_to_extract folder. These notebooks support both modes: zero-shot and few-shot.

The data used is the prepared data, which is generated and stored in a folder after running the script Preparing_data.py. The notebooks illustrate how to use the functions with this data.

Both modes are demonstrated:

Without mentioning the entities to be extracted (BNER)

With mentioning the entities, indicated by the “tip” at the end of the file name

For more details about what “BNER” means, please refer to the paper.